                <pb facs="0601" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 17192.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Griscom.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 29,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Communicate following message at once to the Italian Red Cross through its
                    president, Count Taberna, or other appropriate official: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The American Red Cross desires to tender to the Italian Red Cross its
                            profound sympathy because of the terrible earthquake in Sicily and
                            Calabria. An appeal has been issued by the American Red Cross for
                            contributions for the benefit of the sufferers.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">William H.
                                Taft</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">President of the American Red
                                Gross.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bacon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
